Dragon Blast (2026-11-19): Zandatsu's renut/0032 (Mali parts only, without MGR's widescreen resolve change) and
renut/0036. On three-digit Mali GPUs a scissor change in the middle of a pass was ignored (a small HUD box drawn over the
whole screen): each scissor change closes the pass and the next one opens with the scissor as its render area.
swordman_renut_scissor_pass: auto (default: three-digit Mali), true or false; swordman_renut_scissor_area: exact
(default, Zandatsu's choice after the POCO X7 Pro tests), 16, 64 (widened to Mali tiles) or full. Both read every frame.

diff --git a/app/src/renut_engine/gpu/backend/present.cpp b/app/src/renut_engine/gpu/backend/present.cpp
--- a/app/src/renut_engine/gpu/backend/present.cpp
+++ b/app/src/renut_engine/gpu/backend/present.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,9 @@
